id: pm-brief-v2ts
title: Canonicalize the complete-corpus reader and adopt the current pm host contract
description: "pm-brief still shells out through the removed/deprecated list-all alias with bounded default output and an incomplete package-local receipt decoder. Its development CLI is pinned to 2026.8.15 although 2026.8.21 is current, and manifest.json retains the SDK-ignored top-level compatibility key. Migrate the reader onto canonical list --all with full projection, strict reads, and both output bounds disabled; adopt the public complete-list SDK certification primitive while supplementing any verified fail-open gaps; align manifest and development contracts without inflating the minimum behavior floor."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: agents,canonical-list,completeness,latest-cli,sdk,tdd
created_at: "2026-08-21T06:18:04.769Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T23:07:39.533Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-21T07:12:41.162Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-21T07:12:41.162Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Create red-first tests proving the exact canonical argv and rejection of every independent incomplete, omitted, compacted, malformed, count-inconsistent, blank-ID, and duplicate-ID envelope; Use the public pm SDK complete-list certification primitive and add only behavior-justified supplementary validation for verified SDK gaps; Remove the ignored top-level manifest compatibility key, retain pm_min_version and peer floor 2026.8.15 unless behavior requires a higher minimum, and exact-pin development to pm CLI/SDK 2026.8.21; Update docs, docstrings, generated changelog, package/workflow changelog reads, and all canonical terminology; Run release:check, npm and Bun packed fresh-project acceptance, raw-manifest compatibility at minimum and development hosts, PM validation/reconciliation/duplicate gates, and full tracked/history privacy checks; Create a specific PR, wait for exact-head CI and every available review bot, disposition every artifact, and do not merge or publish while independent quality, privacy, or review gates remain"
definition_of_ready: "Canonical checkout is clean and unique; package and companion trackers show no duplicate item; installed and published pm CLI/SDK version is measured; current reader, manifest, tests, workflows, releases, GitHub reports, and history/privacy baseline are inspected."
risk: high
confidence: 100
reporter: codex
severity: high
repro_steps: Run rg for list-all in index.ts and inspect package.json/manifest.json against installed pm CLI/SDK 2026.8.21; exercise the current public complete-list certifier with missing omission/read-output receipts.
resolution: "Replaced the legacy bounded whole-corpus read with canonical strict full unbounded list output, SDK certification plus verified supplemental receipts, current development dependencies, a proven 2026.8.20 host floor, portable changelog resolution, and mandatory packed npm/Bun acceptance."
expected_result: "Every brief command consumes a fully certified all-status workspace or fails with actionable evidence, emits no deprecated alias diagnostic, uses current SDK primitives and development dependencies, and preserves honest independent release gates."
actual_result: "Release gates pass 270 tests, 76 documented declarations, zero production vulnerabilities, a nine-file pack, and mandatory npm-current, Bun-current, and npm-minimum installed acceptance with valid real-data JSON and zero stderr. Source coverage is 100.00% lines, 92.12% branches, and 100.00% functions, so pm-brief-gtiy remains open. Exact-head CI/security checks are green; CodeRabbit verified all eight fixes in-thread, while its second full pass, Sourcery, Cubic, Greptile, and Gemini have the recorded capacity/silence limitations."
component: complete-corpus reader and host compatibility
