comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-21T06:20:45.450Z","harness:codex","Red-first evidence: npm run build:test passed, then node --test test/brief.test.ts failed 11 complete-reader cases under project-local pm CLI 2026.8.15. The real canonical capture returned ambiguous_list_all for list --all, proving the current development host cannot exercise the new contract. New cases also require failures for missing pagination receipts, contradictory unreadable/omission counts, absent or compacted universal-output receipts, explicit budget truncation, row-count disagreement, blank IDs, and duplicates before production changes."
  "2026-08-21T06:23:18.666Z","harness:codex","Installed SDK 2026.8.21 reproduction: certifyCompleteListResult accepted a real canonical envelope after independently deleting omission_receipt, deleting read_output, setting unreadable_item_count to 1 behind status complete, and making omission count/groups contradict has_omissions=false. PmCompleteListValidationError also suggests stale pm list-all without output-limit unbounded. Upstream pm-cli issue 1078 owns the primitive fix; pm-brief will use the SDK certifier plus narrow supplemental fail-closed checks until a corrected release exists."
notes[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-21T06:41:04.677Z",codex,"TDD evidence: against the old 2026.8.15 host, the exact canonical argv tests failed with ambiguous_list_all. After only upgrading the host, the old decoder accepted missing or contradictory omission/read-output receipts and the bounded real read failed. The production change makes those tests pass without weakening fixtures or suppressing coverage."
  "2026-08-21T06:41:05.058Z",codex,"Installed artifact acceptance: npm/npx emitted 1439 stdout bytes and Bun/bunx emitted 1457 stdout bytes; both were valid JSON, included the created fixture item, exited zero, and emitted zero stderr bytes. Temporary acceptance projects and the generated untracked Bun lock were moved to trash after verification."
  "2026-08-21T06:44:01.318Z",codex,"Direct minimum-host acceptance: npm-executed @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.20 ran the exact production canonical list argv against this 56-item tracker and returned completeness.status=complete with omission_receipt.has_omissions=false. This proves 2026.8.20, rather than the rejected 2026.8.15 baseline, is the narrow behavior floor."
  "2026-08-21T06:45:25.675Z",codex,PR #76 opened from f804590 as the implementation and review record. It explicitly states that exact coverage pm-brief-gtiy remains open and blocks merge/publication.
  "2026-08-21T06:58:54.902Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round 1 raised eight findings. Accepted: explicit shipped-release attribution, complete linked acceptance commands, packed extension execution on the declared 2026.8.20 host, shared signal formatting, Windows-safe pm-changelog resolution, lazy real-envelope test construction, machine-code-only upstream failure assertion, and a shared non-test version contract. The requested reopen was replaced with release=2026.8.14 because lifecycle completion is true and explicit release metadata is the correct --respect-item-release contract."
  "2026-08-21T07:12:40.587Z",codex,"Review closure snapshot for implementation head d9bfe79a9557fce20eb993c108bf22282d2d7842: Node 22, Node 26, Windows audit, Semgrep, DeepScan, and Hound are green. CodeRabbit first reviewed the prior head with eight findings; every finding was fixed, replied to, upvoted, and individually re-verified by CodeRabbit on d9bfe79 with all threads resolved. Its requested fresh full pass was rate-limited and explicitly acknowledged as a limitation, not approval. Sourcery is weekly-quota limited/skipped, Cubic skipped, and Greptile/Gemini remained silent through the review window; none is counted as approval. Exact coverage item pm-brief-gtiy remains in progress and blocks merge/publication."
  "2026-08-21T23:07:39.483Z","harness:ox-alpha","merged PR #76 as c5d3d541f8768b2de7692bc52a37fcb1a4721558, all threads resolved, checks green, release workflow Daily Release active (schedule-triggered; CI push run in progress on main)"
